WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.678
Chapter six. Gold: is there money without a cave?

00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:11.742
Every money in this episode had a Wren. A ship on Yap. Glass from Venice.

00:00:11.742 --> 00:00:15.792
Iron drills. Shells from Zanzibar. A mint in Rome.

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:20.815
Each time, money got easier to make. Usually, the savers paid.

00:00:21.765 --> 00:00:22.424
Now gold.

00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:27.990
All the gold ever mined would fit in one cube, about 23 metres on each side.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.823
As tall as a seven-storey building. Almost all of it still exists.

00:00:33.173 --> 00:00:38.388
Each year, the world's mines add a slice on top, less than half a metre thick.

00:00:38.388 --> 00:00:38.990
Under 2%.

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:45.767
Gold had its rushes. California in 1849, then Australia.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.635
In the 1850s, the world dug over three

00:00:48.635 --> 00:00:51.805
times as much gold a year as in the 1840s.

00:00:51.805 --> 00:00:55.353
Three times a thin slice is still a thin slice.

00:00:55.703 --> 00:01:00.702
Prices rose. In Britain, where money was gold, by up to a third.

00:01:00.702 --> 00:01:05.076
They stayed high for about twenty years. Then they fell.

00:01:05.076 --> 00:01:08.825
By the 1890s, they were lower than in the 1840s.

00:01:09.775 --> 00:01:15.561
Compare. Cowries: a silver dollar cost 10 times more shells. Rome:

00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:20.120
wheat cost 37 times more. Gold, in the great rushes:

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.714
prices up to a third higher, for a while.

00:01:23.714 --> 00:01:27.396
Gold came closest to money without a cave.

00:01:28.746 --> 00:01:35.141
And today? In ten years, gold's price roughly tripled, with big swings.

00:01:35.141 --> 00:01:41.355
So digging it pays far more. Still, mine output grew under 1% a year.

00:01:41.355 --> 00:01:43.967
Nobody has found gold's cave.

00:01:45.716 --> 00:01:51.012
Our money today isn't gold. So who is its Wren? First:

00:01:51.012 --> 00:01:56.209
why is gold so hard to flood? Next episode: why gold.

